            "# Portfolio Codebase Audit — Jonathan Verdun\n\n**Date:** 2026-04-22  \n**Branch:** `main` @ `b3d39ce`  \n**Overall Score: 7.2 / 10**\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Project Structure](#1-project-structure)\n2. [Tech Stack](#2-tech-stack)\n3. [Architecture](#3-architecture)\n4. [Performance](#4-performance)\n5. [Accessibility](#5-accessibility)\n6. [SEO](#6-seo)\n7. [Testing](#7-testing)\n8. [Code Quality](#8-code-quality)\n9. [WebGL & Animation](#9-webgl--animation)\n10. [Mobile & Responsiveness](#10-mobile--responsiveness)\n11. [Build & DevOps](#11-build--devops)\n12. [Priority Improvements](#12-priority-improvements)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Structure\n\n```\njonathan-verdun-portfolio/\n├── src/\n│   ├── app/\n│   │   ├── layout.tsx          # Root layout + ProjectProvider + metadata\n│   │   ├── page.tsx            # Main portfolio page (~220 LOC)\n│   │   └── globals.css         # CSS variables + utility classes\n│   ├── components/\n│   │   ├── hooks/              # useProjects, useTerminal\n│   │   ├── BioinformaticsGraphic.tsx\n│   │   ├── Terminal.tsx\n│   │   ├── ProjectGallery.tsx\n│   │   ├── ProjectCard.tsx\n│   │   ├── InteractiveTopology.tsx\n│   │   ├── TopologyMesh.tsx\n│   │   ├── PAdicBackground.tsx\n│   │   └── ErrorBoundary.tsx\n│   ├── lib/\n│   │   ├── contracts/          # Domain types + contracts (*.types.ts pattern)\n│   │   ├── services/           # CommandProcessor, ProjectRepository\n│   │   ├── shaders/            # GLSL in TopologyShaders.ts\n│   │   ├── animations.ts       # Framer Motion variant factory\n│   │   ├── siteConfig.ts       # SEO & metadata\n│   │   └── uiConfig.ts         # UI token mappings\n│   └── __tests__/              # 7 test files, ~222 LOC\n├── .github/workflows/ci.yml\n├── Dockerfile + docker-compose.yml\n└── docs/                       # TypeDoc-generated output\n```\n\n**Strengths:** Clean separation of concerns — contracts define domain types, services implement business logic, components are pure UI, hooks bridge the two. The `.types.ts` convention is consistently applied.\n\n**Concern:** `page.tsx` uses `'use client'` at the root page level, which disables RSC-level streaming and data fetching for the entire page.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n\n| Layer           | Technology                             | Version       |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| Framework       | Next.js (App Router)                   | 16.1.6        |\n| UI              | React                                  | 19.2.3        |\n| Language        | TypeScript (strict)                    | 5.x           |\n| Styling         | Tailwind CSS v4 + PostCSS              | 4.x           |\n| Animations      | Framer Motion                          | 12.34.0       |\n| 3D / WebGL      | Three.js + @react-three/fiber          | 0.183 / 9.5.0 |\n| Post-processing | @react-three/postprocessing            | 3.0.4         |\n| Icons           | Lucide React                           | 0.563.0       |\n| Testing         | Jest 30 + Testing Library + fast-check | 30.2.0        |\n| Docs            | TypeDoc                                | 0.28.16       |\n| Linting         | ESLint 9 + Prettier 3                  | 9.x / 3.8.1   |\n| Git hooks       | Husky + lint-staged                    | 9.x / 16.x    |\n| Compiler        | Babel React Compiler                   | 1.0.0         |\n\n**Large bundle contributors:**\n\n- `three` — ~650 KB (tree-shaken in practice)\n- `framer-motion` — ~40 KB gzipped\n- `@react-three/fiber` + `drei` — ~60 KB gzipped\n\n---\n\n## 3. Architecture\n\n**Pattern: SOLID-Compliant Service-Oriented + React Context**\n\n```\nComponents (UI)\n    │\n    ├── Custom Hooks (useProjects, useTerminal)\n    │       │\n    │       └── Services (CommandProcessor, ProjectRepository)\n    │               │\n    │               └── Contracts / Domain Types\n    │\n    └── ErrorBoundary (class component, lifecycle-safe)\n```\n\n**What works well:**\n\n- `ICommandProcessor` interface enables dependency injection in tests\n- `ProjectProvider` / `useProjects` pattern cleanly separates data from display\n- `animations.ts` as a variant factory eliminates scattered Framer Motion configs\n- `siteConfig` and `uiConfig` centralize magic strings and tokens\n\n**What to address:**\n\n- `page.tsx` marks the entire route `'use client'` — consider splitting into a server shell with client islands\n- No React `Suspense` boundary around Three.js (if WebGL init hangs, nothing is shown)\n- `ErrorBoundary` only catches render errors; async errors in hooks go unhandled\n\n---\n\n## 4. Performance\n\n### Score: 6.5 / 10\n\n**Implemented optimizations:**\n\n- React Compiler (`reactCompiler: true`) for automatic memoization\n- `antialias: false` and `multisampling={0}` on the WebGL canvas\n- `dpr={[1, 2]}` dynamic pixel ratio\n- Post-processing at reduced height (300px)\n- `useMemo` for shader geometry in `TopologyMesh`\n- `useRef` for DOM access to avoid re-renders\n\n**Performance gaps:**\n\n| Issue                                                                                \n\n[Content truncated...]",
